## Resolution

- `nrl/tools/check_reference.py` verifies the archive hash and all 54 manifest payload entries, extracts to a fresh directory and records an optional test run without overwriting existing data.
- The unchanged Python suite ran on 2026-10-25: **64 passed, zero skipped**, including the five random tiny-Qwen integration cases. The full protocol and package versions are in `nrl/reports/reference-2026-10-25.json`; there was no pretrained-model download or evaluation.
- `nrl/tools/generate_fixtures.py` generated and then byte-checked `nrl/tests/fixtures/f64-v0.json` against verified original source. Its SHA-256 is `21853060ca335db5c7fc8366ad62e1b56cb89c93f507cfc4dfc1bb847f0f4fa0`.
- `docs/nrl/reference-inventory.md` records repeat commands, provenance, current ABI 20 APIs, and limits. `nrl/reference/requirements-cpu.lock` pins the environment actually run; it is not a wheel hash lock.
- This completes T00 on the NRL branch. The code and data still require the project's code landing gate; no OS, hardware or native NRL execution is claimed.
